Z||000000||mblackwell||07-04-2001||05:34 AM||||My battery is dying.  This battery came with my car, and I am pretty sure it is less than 3 years old.  It says on the battery that there is a 3 year replacemnet warranty.  Its a higher quality Duralast.  Will any retail place give me a free new one even though I dont have any papers or recipts for it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||07-04-2001||05:56 AM||||Usually those warranties are on a pro rated basis and most places require receipts. At best you would get $3 off on a new one. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-04-2001||11:46 AM||||Yeah, most batterys are only free replacement for the first year. Then after that they pro rate it on a monthly basis.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||07-04-2001||12:01 PM||||is it autozone who caries duralast? <BR>many companies understand  you cant keep a reciept for 3 years.  take it where they sell duralast.  they can look at the manufactured date on the battery.  you might get something.  <BR>autozone keeps there records in the computer, so it may be inthere from the original owner,  i dont know.  the premium battery at autozone carries a 3 year free replacement warranty. i think its the duralast gold.  they also have a one and a two year warranty battery<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
